    <string name="guide_p1">AlAzharTex is the offline stock book of AlAzhar Textiles — every fabric roll, colour, shed and movement is stored on this device. No internet, no account server, no data leaves the phone.</string>
    <string name="guide_p2">The admin manages every shed, the masters catalogue, settings and backups. Keepers manage the sheds assigned to them and may read the others. The sales manager reads everything and changes nothing.</string>
    <string name="guide_p3">Everything works with zero connectivity. Backups are your responsibility: export the database from Settings and keep the file plus its sha256 sidecar somewhere safe.</string>
    <string name="guide_p4">Export writes a consistent snapshot (VACUUM INTO) with a sha256 sidecar and a share or save sheet. Import runs a five-rung integrity ladder (hash, SQLite header, PRAGMA integrity_check, schema and app version, per-table manifest counts) before you confirm a destructive overwrite; a safety copy of the current database is kept.</string>
    <string name="guide_p5">Dates are always yyyy-mm-dd. &quot;Today&quot; is Cairo time. Numbers use Western digits by default; you may switch to Arabic-Indic digits in Settings. A utilisation gauge is green below fifty percent, amber from fifty to eighty-five percent, red above eighty-five percent — and wh-625 is deliberately over capacity as the scale test.</string>
    <string name="guide_p6">Where is my data? In the app&#8217;s private storage on this device only; export regularly. That single answer covers most support calls.</string>

